{
  "requirement": "No prompt, tool result, or tool error the harness gives the model MUST state a\nline number or line range of a project source, except within source text it\nquotes and where a tool error repeats a line number the model supplied. The\nharness MUST identify a source location by file and outline selector under\n{cite}`requirements.references.outline_selectors` instead.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `requirements.authoring.no_line_numbers`**\n1. No tool result may state a line number or range of a project source. This covers `habeas` reads, `ripgrep`, `outline`, `references` and the mandatory inputs.\n2. No prompt may state one. This covers the subject message, including a site's matches, and the tool descriptions.\n3. No tool error may state one, except where it repeats a number the model supplied.\n4. Source locations are given by file and outline selector.\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- **`habeas` results.**\n  - `reading_records_only_delivered_sources_and_their_terms` asserts that a selector read and an EOF line-range read carry no `line_start` or `line_end`. It also asserts that recorded inputs equal the selector-only `outline_input`.\n  - `line_range_reads_record_the_innermost_covering_nodes` asserts no `line_start` or `line_end` on nested-node, whole-file and plain-text range reads. The items are identified by selectors such as `fn[first]`, `mod[inner]/fn[second]` and `line@…`.\n- **`ripgrep` results.** `search_merges_context_windows_and_respects_ignore_rules` asserts that entries have no `line_start` and that each line object has no `line` key. `separate_windows_in_one_node_are_divided_by_an_elision_line` asserts the exact entry shape, with only text and matched flags and an elision marker between windows.\n- **`outline` results.** `outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs` asserts the exact selector, kind, name and children output, and that plain-text entries have no `line_start`.\n- **`references` results.** `references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs` compares the whole result by equality. Each site has only name, role, file and item, so any extra line field would fail.\n- **Mandatory inputs.** `anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs` asserts the exact input JSON, which has file, item, hash, kind and text and no line fields. The site-review test asserts the exact subject message against the approved prompt, with matches given as kind, query and item. `sites_are_the_innermost_nodes_of_site_matches_and_violations_within_them` asserts `matches_value()` has the same selector-only shape.\n- **Tool descriptions.** `submission_descriptions_explain_arguments_and_successful_completion` asserts that the submit tools' descriptions contain \"outline selectors\" and \"never line numbers\".\n- **Tool errors.**\n  - `tool_errors_drop_the_source_line_of_a_parse_error` unit-tests `without_source_lines`. It covers the parse-error position forms (a `line N:` prefix and an `at line N, column M` suffix), the `file:N:` diagnostic form and the \"first declared at\" path-position form. Each is rewritten to the `file#` selector. It also checks that both the single-number and the range forms of the \"is not an inclusive range\" error keep the numbers the model gave.\n  - `tool_errors_give_the_model_no_line_numbers_it_did_not_supply` runs end to end. A read with a `line_start` past the end of the file yields an error starting with the file and that supplied start number followed by \"is not an inclusive range\", so only the supplied number is repeated. A parse error on a broken file names its line when dispatched directly. The request delivered to the model through `assess` contains \"cannot parse\" and no `line N: ` text.\n\n**Exceptions and gaps considered**\n- The \"model supplied\" exception is tested in both forms, a single number and a range.\n- The \"quoted source text\" exception needs no test of its own. Source text is returned unchanged, and the tests assert exact `text` arrays.\n- I found no scenario the requirement names that is untested. Other tool-error formats fall under the same `without_source_lines` implementation, and the tested diagnostic shapes cover the distinct patterns it handles.\n\nI found no gap.",
  "references": "5f07d59d3d70ca6a503110d2a797133c2b9f1eafd54fb53e7ee2fb02587ec51a",
